:) Not in my native language/dialect.

It bothers me that Lojban doesn't have a true H, except one that
can only interpose two vowels.

I see that names like la xustyn. (Houston) and la xavanas. (Havana)
all start with x, so I guess that is the right way.

As a side note, Lojban's x sounds more like a k to me than it
sounds like an h. My dialect of English doesn't have that x sound.

For example, we tend to Anglicize "Bach" as "Bak," not "Bahh." (In
fact, a terminal h is not really pronounced at all I guess -- it
just lengthens the vowel.)

